{"name":"Gazebo Grey","hex":"#d1d0cb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gazebo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A belvedere, either a type of summer-house or a roofed, detached porch-like structure, usually in a yard, park or lawn.","A dismountable shelter comprising a roof or awning supported by poles, and often having removable sides; a canopy tent"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gazebo"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gazebo","blocks":[{"text":"A gazebo is a pavilion structure, sometimes octagonal or turret-shaped, often built in a park, garden, or spacious public area. Some are used on occasions as bandstands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/%D0%93%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%B4_%D0%A0%D0%90%D0%9D%2C_%D1%81%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%B1%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%80._Moscow%2C_Russia._-_panoramio_-_Oleg_Yu.Novikov.jpg/330px-%D0%93%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%B9_%D0%B1%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%B4_%D0%A0%D0%90%D0%9D%2C_%D1%81%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%B1%D0%BE%D1%82%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%87%D0%B5%D1%80._Moscow%2C_Russia._-_panoramio_-_Oleg_Yu.Novikov.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gazebo","wikidata":"Q961082"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Victorian_Gazebo.jpg/500px-Victorian_Gazebo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Victorian_Gazebo.jpg/1280px-Victorian_Gazebo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Victorian_Gazebo.jpg/500px-Victorian_Gazebo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Victorian-style bandstand gazebo at Fellows Riverside Gardens at Mill Creek Park, Youngstown, Ohio","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVictorian_Gazebo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Rainy_day_at_Camp_Horno%2C_Camp_Pendleton.png/500px-Rainy_day_at_Camp_Horno%2C_Camp_Pendleton.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Rainy_day_at_Camp_Horno%2C_Camp_Pendleton.png/1280px-Rainy_day_at_Camp_Horno%2C_Camp_Pendleton.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Rainy_day_at_Camp_Horno%2C_Camp_Pendleton.png/500px-Rainy_day_at_Camp_Horno%2C_Camp_Pendleton.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tent gazebo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARainy_day_at_Camp_Horno%2C_Camp_Pendleton.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/NYBG_Rose_Garden.jpg/500px-NYBG_Rose_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/NYBG_Rose_Garden.jpg/1280px-NYBG_Rose_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/NYBG_Rose_Garden.jpg/500px-NYBG_Rose_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gazebo is a focal point of the Peggy Rockefeller Rose Garden in the New York Botanical Garden. The garden layout, including the design for an iron-lattice gazebo and surrounding fence, was created by the renowned landscape architect Beatrix Farrand in 1916. Due to iron shortages during World War I, construction of the gazebo and the fence was not completed, and the whole design was later forgotten. In the mid-1980s, Farrand's original plans were rediscovered. David Rockefeller donated $1 million for the completion of Farrand's design, and the garden, including the gazebo and the fence, was finally realized in 1988. It was named the \"Peggy Rockefeller Rose Garden\" after David's wife and NYBG Board member  Margaret \"Peggy\" McGrath Rockefeller.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANYBG_Rose_Garden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Spitz_Pavillon_Hinterhaus-3233.jpg/330px-Spitz_Pavillon_Hinterhaus-3233.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Spitz_Pavillon_Hinterhaus-3233.jpg/960px-Spitz_Pavillon_Hinterhaus-3233.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Spitz_Pavillon_Hinterhaus-3233.jpg/330px-Spitz_Pavillon_Hinterhaus-3233.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpitz_Pavillon_Hinterhaus-3233.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikime